I need to update the vitest config to pass Babel options to the `react()` plugin so that it uses `@babel/preset-typescript`. Looking at the plugin code, I need to pass:
```typescript
react({
  babel: {
    presets: [
      ['@babel/preset-typescript', { isTSX: true, allExtensions: true }]
    ]
  }
})
```

But there's a catch - the plugin loads plugins from its own loaded plugins map. Looking at `createBabelOptions`:
```javascript
for (const [preset, options] of rawOptions.presets) {
  const presetModule = typeof preset === 'function' ? preset : loadedPresets.get(preset);
  if (!presetModule) continue;
  ...
}
if (typeof preset !== 'function' && !loadedPresets.has(preset)) {
  continue;
}
```

So the plugin only loads presets from its internal map unless they're functions. The `canSkipBabel` check ensures Babel runs when there are presets configured, so if I add `@babel/preset-typescript` as a function instead, it won't be skipped and Babel will handle the TypeScript transformation properly.

Good. `@babel/preset-typescript` has a CJS main export. Let me try to pass it as a function to the react plugin. I'll update the vitest config to use:
```typescript
