```

This means if I pass `babel` as a function, it gets called with the file `id` and `ssr` flag to generate the options dynamically. The presets and plugins I return get added to the config, so I could dynamically load `@babel/preset-typescript` that way. Or I could just use the object form and reference the preset directly from the loaded plugins map.

Let me think through how the plugin actually processes these options...

```

javascript
} else {
  const { presets, plugins } = createBabelOptions(opts.babel);
  newBabelOptions.presets.push(...presets);
